# WuLab release workspace

Read `skill/wulab-research/SKILL.md` and its five model files when doing research. Follow the assigned role and use simple language. For software work, read `README.md` and the relevant code before editing.

Keep private state in `.wulab/`, project work in `projects/ID/workspace/`, and shared material in `library/` and `data/`. Never include credentials or private research data in a public commit.

The example is isolated: its meetings are scripted, while its synthetic experiment can be rerun. Do not report it as evidence of an actual autonomous agent run. Creating a demo or running tests does not authorize paid research.

Use the saved task service for active teams. Preserve completed work, genuine scientific uncertainty, and director holds when fixing an obstacle. Report what was tested and any remaining compatibility limits.
